{
  "v": 11,
  "label": "a round of two pages parked by a mass absence keeps the checkpoint its first page carried",
  "note": "the round opens under the first page, which carries the checkpoint c1 and a cursor; the last page, carrying none, finds all 20 based bindings in scope absent, more than half of at least 20, so the round parks: its last page lands as a page before the last, no cursor, and the checkpoint the round holds stays the first page's, the last page carrying none to record (SYNC.md §4, §5; STORAGE.md §10). The round's id is not stated: an engine may draw it anew at the park so the next listing, from the first page, stamps under an id the parked one did not",
